Tendon outgrowth and attachment to an ectopic bone was observed in 7 of 9 samples and in samples with one dorsal element, the regenerated tendon wrapped around the P2 stump and attached to the ectopic dorsal bone (Supplementary Fig
6B
).

However, one of the digits displayed a milder chondrogenic response that was not associated with the peripheral callus but was distal to the amputated stump and formed a cavity between the stump and the regenerated chondrogenic element (Fig.
3e, f
).
